{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"8bd792f0e31ec925","name":"card_event_long_range_desert_group","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Breakthrough/events/card_event_long_range_desert_group","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"LONG RANGE DESERT GROUP","text":"Your units get: \"When this unit deals damage to a unit, destroy it.\"","flavorText":"The Long Range Desert Group (LRDG) was a special operations unit of the British Army during WWII. This was an elite unit that specialized in long range reconnaissance missions, intelligence gathering and raiding operations. The unit was founded in Egypt in 1940 and was only made up of volunteers who were recruited from all the Commonwealth forces. The unit consisted of 14 patrols, 15-20 men in each, and each patrol usually operated in Chevrolet 30 cwt unarmored trucks and a Willy Jeep for the commanding officer. The LRDG was part of the Western Desert Force Eighth Army between 1940-43 and their area of operations stretched about 1500 km over the Sahara desert. Their mission was to provide critical intelligence to Allied commanders and finding new paths for Allied armor for flank maneuvers, but they were perhaps better known for their cooperation with the newly established SAS that were operating behind enemy lines. In 1943 the LRDG was retrained for mountain warfare and for the remainder of the war they operated in Italy and the Balkans where they continued to support the Allied onslaught against the Axis.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_long_range_desert_group","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_long_range_desert_group_title","SourceString":"LONG RANGE DESERT GROUP","LocalizedString":"LONG RANGE DESERT GROUP"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_long_range_desert_gro