orce Eighth Army between 1940-43 and their area of operations stretched about 1500 km over the Sahara desert. Their mission was to provide critical intelligence to Allied commanders and finding new paths for Allied armor for flank maneuvers, but they were perhaps better known for their cooperation with the newly established SAS that were operating behind enemy lines. In 1943 the LRDG was retrained for mountain warfare and for the remainder of the war they operated in Italy and the Balkans where they continued to support the Allied onslaught against the Axis."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamage"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'For_the_Queen'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/For_the_Queen.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Breakthrough/t_lrdg.t_lrdg","SubPathString":""},"artist":"David Pentland","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/LONG_RANGE_DESERT_GROUP.LONG_RANGE_DESERT_GROUP","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":256.0},"historyPhotoSource":"Imperial War Museum","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_long_range_desert_group_photo","SourceString":"The Long Range Desert Group on patrol in the African Western Desert, 1942. ","LocalizedString":"The Long Range Desert Group on patrol in the African Western Desert, 1942. "},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_long_range_desert_group","owner":"card_event_long_range_desert_group_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{